---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { readReader } from '../lib/reader/cookies';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
const reader = readReader(Astro.cookies, Astro.url.protocol === 'https:');
---
<BaseLayout title={`Editorial policy · ${SITE.name}`} description="What PulseNSFW covers for people who watch." reader={reader}>
  <article class="page" style="padding-bottom:48px">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Editorial policy' }]} />
    <p class="kicker">Policy</p>
    <h1>Editorial policy</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Pulse is for porn consumers. It covers stars and creators worth watching, sites, AI chat and generators, toys, VR, adult games, guides, top lists, and news a viewer would actually use: new scenes, new sites and apps, star news, and deals.</p>
      <p>Studio business, platform policy, and tools for running a page are out. So are exploitation, nonconsensual material, and harassment.</p>
      <p>Drafts stay drafts until a fact check. Claims about a product, price, platform, or person get a source URL and a checked date in the entity record. Articles reference entities by slug; they do not keep a second copy of the facts. The publishing keys for the agent desk never ship to the browser.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
